Screen Scanner / FacetSensus

The current manuscript is FACETSENSUS.md at the repository root.

The architecture investigates scene geometry and surface appearance from calibrated measurements across a sensing matrix, illumination states and registered panel poses. Planar integrated receivers, dual-function pixels and multi-region optical responses are candidates. A pyramid carrier is not a prerequisite.

In the reversible-pixel implementation, roles are assigned to whole pixels. A receiving pixel reads all its sensing regions separately while other pixels may illuminate the scene. Prompt active reflections must arrive during reception. Detector values are mixed optical measurements, not automatically focused image coordinates or depth.

Geometry and texture must be estimated using the calibrated measurement operator, visibility, spectral response and illumination. Observed appearance, intrinsic reflectance and inferred completion are distinct. New registered observations update the scene state; they need not retrain a fixed learned model.

This is a research concept. The included calculations are limited examples and do not demonstrate a fabricated sensor or textured environment reconstruction.
